ngs.", "Incumbent Dina Titus (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Dina Titus seeks another term in a Las Vegas-area district that leans about two points Democratic, in an environment that has favored her party this cycle. She holds a cash-on-hand advantage and has drawn mostly Safe or Likely Democratic ratings from professional forecasters, with prediction markets pricing her win probability in the low-to-mid nineties.\n\nRepublicans landed a serious recruit in state senator Carrie Buck, who has out-raised Titus and benefits from national attention to the race, including the 'no tax on tips' issue in a tourism-heavy district. Still, the absence of public polling and Titus's incumbency edge keep the race clearly on the Democratic side of the ledger, with room for movement if the national environment shifts.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9567, "margin": 11.7}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9528, "margin": 11.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9532, "margin": 11.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9485, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9322, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9231, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9459, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9435, "margin": 10.5}]}